>
> Were games like the Zadir game the reason that NAO recently implemented
> the Z-scores ranking system alongside the traditional high-scores
> ranking?  There's no macro for ascending, obviously :).

AFAICT, Z-scores had been introduced recently because some people here
felt that plain scores being an inappropriate metric to measure the
Nethack playing skills.

The simple score values will have highscore-"farming" players/games on
top of the list while people that ascend, for example fast (in few
turns with low score) or people that ascend often without explicitly
considering their score value, will not even enter the highscore
table.

The Z-score will reward ascensions and diversity of played classes,
because subsequent ascensions of the same class count less.

